course: dictionary
lesson: 4704
title: Honeymoon and the happy start
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A honeymoon is a holiday that a newly married couple take together just after their wedding. Read the context: «A honeymoon is a holiday a couple takes just after the wedding, to rest and celebrate, just the two of them.» The clues are just after the wedding and just the two of them, so the meaning is a couple's holiday after marrying.
explain: The word can also mean the happy, easy time at the start of something new, like a new job or a new leader, before problems begin. When you read «the honeymoon period» about a new prime minister or teacher, ask: does a holiday fit here? It does not, so the word must mean that early happy time.
explain: Honeymoon can also be a verb: to honeymoon is to go on a honeymoon. Look out for phrases like «go on honeymoon», «on their honeymoon» and «the honeymoon is over», which means the happy start has come to an end.
explain: A honeymoon follows a wedding, but not every couple marries. «Some couples get engaged, which is a promise to marry, then plan a wedding, and after it go away on a honeymoon; some couples never marry but stay together, and all of these are normal.» Use the context to see what the word belongs to.
fact: A honeymoon is a holiday that a newly married couple take together just after the wedding.
fact: The honeymoon period is the happy, easy time at the start of something new, before problems begin.
fact: «The honeymoon is over» means the happy start has come to an end.
fact: Honeymoon can be a verb: honeymoon, honeymooned, honeymooning.
fact: Engaged means you have promised to marry, and a wedding comes later.
exercise: «A honeymoon is a holiday a couple takes just after the wedding.» What is a honeymoon? | A long journey to work | A party for guests after a wedding | *A holiday a newly married couple take together after their wedding | A honey shop in the hills
exercise: A new teacher has a «honeymoon period». What does this mean? | A time when the teacher is ill | A holiday for the children | *The happy, easy start before problems begin | The end of the school year
exercise: Which form of the verb means they went on a honeymoon in the past? | honeymoon | honeymooning | *honeymooned | honeymoons
test: The phrase «the honeymoon is over» most likely means | The wedding was cancelled | *The happy, easy start has ended and problems begin | The holiday was very long | The couple has just got married
test: «Some couples never marry but stay together, and all of these are normal.» What does this tell us? | Couples who never marry cannot go on honeymoon | *Not every couple marries, and that is normal | Engaged couples always stay together for life | Every couple must get married
exam: In «the honeymoon period» for a new leader, what does honeymoon mean? | A wedding party | A period of bad weather | A holiday for the leader | *The happy, easy time at the start of the new role
